  "term": "varicella-zoster",
  "definition": "Varicella-zoster is an acute infection, usually limited in duration, thought to result from reactivation of dormant varicella-zoster virus after an earlier case of chickenpox. It affects sensory nerve ganglia and the skin areas they supply, causing severe nerve pain and clusters of small blisters along the involved nerve.",
